# Security & integrity (non-negotiable)

- TLS everywhere. Passwords hashed with Argon2 (fallback bcrypt).
- QR verification is 100% server-side. Never compute member/discount/ticket
  validity client-side.
  - Membership QR = user_id + signed token.
  - Ticket QR = user_id + event_id + unique tamper-proof token.
- Rate-limit QR scans in Redis: max 10/min/user.
- Never store raw card data; rely on gateway tokenization. No payment info on device.
- ID/passport images + nationality are sensitive PII: encrypt at rest, restrict
  access, apply a retention policy.
- All admin actions write to an immutable audit log (who/what/when).
- Money stored as integer minor units or Decimal — never float.
- All datetimes UTC; convert only at the edges.
- Multi-step writes use DB transactions. Payment ops use idempotency keys.
- Enforce hard caps (e.g., gathering ≤ 20 attendees) atomically in the DB layer.